  "operative_text": "Section 48986(a) (Education Code (added)): 48986. (a) (1) A local educational agency shall inform, through a notice in the manner prescribed in this section, the parents or guardians of each enrolled pupil of California’s child access prevention laws and laws relating to the safe storage of firearms, including, but not limited to, Division 4 (commencing with Section 25000) of Title 4 of Part 6 of the Penal Code. (2) The notice shall be provided annually at the beginning of the first semester or quarter of the regular school term. (3) The notice shall be informed by the most updated model language developed pursuant to subdivision (c).\nSection 48986(b)(2) (Education Code (added)): (2) A school district shall provide the notice as part of the annual notification required pursuant to Section 48980.\nSection 48986(c)(1) (Education Code (added)): (c) (1) On or before July 1, 2023, the department shall develop, in consultation with the Department of Justice, model language for the notice described in subdivision (a)."
}